      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "The use of antipsychotics can lead to the development of obesity, dyslipidemia, hypertension and hyperglycemia, risk factors for diabetes mellitus type 2 and cardiovascular diseases."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIM",
          "content": "To find out whether patients suffering from psychoses and schizophrenia and taking antipsychotics should be monitored systematically and periodically for the risk factors for and complications of the above-mentioned diseases."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHOD",
          "content": "A written survey was conducted among the relatives of users of antipsychotics, relatives being members of the Ypsilon association in the Limburg region."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Seventy-eight relatives (27%) returned the forms. Compared to the Dutch population, the risk factor for high blood pressure was remarkably common in the 20-30 age group. In the group of persons aged 30-40 obesity occurred surprisingly frequently; remarkably frequent too was diabetes in the 40-50 age group. At each monitoring session 27% of the users were checked on all parameters. Only 59% of the users were checked periodically."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Apparently, systematic and regular monitoring of risk factors and somatic complications is currently inadequate. The regional survey therefore needs to be extended so that it covers the entire country."
        }
      ]},
